            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "#Cut the copper wire. You need two strands about 1.5 feet (0.4572 m) long.<br><br>[[Image:Make a Light Bulb Step 1 Version 2.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Remove 1\" (2.54 cm) of shielding from the ends of both strands.<br><br>[[Image:Make a Light Bulb Step 2 Version 2.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Use the nail to pierce two holes into the cork. The holes should be in the middle of the cork about 1\" (2.54 cm) apart.<br><br>[[Image:Make a Light Bulb Step 3 Version 2.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Hold the two copper strands parallel to each other in the air.<br><br>[[Image:Make a Light Bulb Step 4 Version 2.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Place one end of each strand 2\" (5cm) inside the two holes drilled into the cork.<br><br>[[Image:Make a Light Bulb Step 5 Version 2.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Bend the end of the two strands inside the cork into a hook shape. The hook of each strand should curve the same way.<br><br>[[Image:Make a Light Bulb Step 6 Version 2.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Cut the iron wire into 1-1/2 to 2 inch (3.8cm to 5cm) strips. Make five strips.<br><br>[[Image:Make a Light Bulb Step 7 Version 2.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Twist the five iron wire lengths together with your fingers.<br><br>[[Image:Make a Light Bulb Step 8 Version 2.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Place the twisted iron wires onto the copper hooks, making sure it touches both copper strands.<br><br>[[Image:Make a Light Bulb Step 9 Version 2.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Put the cork stopper into the glass jar.<br><br>[[Image:Make a Light Bulb Step 10 Version 2.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    "#Take one strand of the copper wire not in the glass jar and wrap the end around one end of the battery. Repeat this for the other strand of copper wire and the other end of the battery.<br><br>[[Image:Make a Light Bulb Step 11 Version 2.jpg|center|550px]]",
                    ""
                ],
                "removed": [
                    "#Cut the copper wire. You need two strands about 1.5 feet (0.4572 m) long.[[Image:Make a Light Bulb Step 1 Version 2.jpg|center|300px]]",
                    "#Remove 1\" (2.54 cm) of shielding from the ends of both strands.[[Image:Make a Light Bulb Step 2 Version 2.jpg|center|300px]]",
                    "#Use the nail to pierce two holes into the cork. The holes should be in the middle of the cork about 1\" (2.54 cm) apart.[[Image:Make a Light Bulb Step 3 Version 2.jpg|center|300px]]",
                    "#Hold the two copper strands parallel to each other in the air.[[Image:Make a Light Bulb Step 4 Version 2.jpg|center|300px]]",
                    "#Place one end of each strand 2\" (5cm) inside the two holes drilled into the cork.[[Image:Make a Light Bulb Step 5 Version 2.jpg|center|300px]]",
                    "#Bend the end of the two strands inside the cork into a hook shape. The hook of each strand should curve the same way.[[Image:Make a Light Bulb Step 6 Version 2.jpg|center|300px]]",
                    "#Cut the iron wire into 1-1/2 to 2 inch (3.8cm to 5cm) strips. Make five strips.[[Image:Make a Light Bulb Step 7 Version 2.jpg|center|300px]]",
                    "#Twist the five iron wire lengths together with your fingers.[[Image:Make a Light Bulb Step 8 Version 2.jpg|center|300px]]",
                    "#Place the twisted iron wires onto the copper hooks, making sure it touches both copper strands.[[Image:Make a Light Bulb Step 9 Version 2.jpg|center|300px]]",
                    "#Put the cork stopper into the glass jar.[[Image:Make a Light Bulb Step 10 Version 2.jpg|center|300px]]",
                    "#Take one strand of the copper wire not in the glass jar and wrap the end around one end of the battery. Repeat this for the other strand of copper wire and the other end of the battery.[[Image:Make a Light Bulb Step 11 Version 2.jpg|center|300px]]"
                ]
            }
