            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "[[Image:Light bulb.jpg|thumb|right|251px]]A light bulb is made when metal filament is heated to the point at which the wire glows. The most well-known type of light bulb is the incandescent light bulb, which is the version used in most homes. Use these steps for making a homemade light bulb.",
                    "",
                    "",
                    "",
                    "* If the light bulb doesn't light up after you've connected the copper ends to the battery, check your connections.",
                    "* Using more than 5 iron strands to make your filament will increase the brightness of your homemade light bulb.",
                    "* Do not touch the filament after it has been lit. It will be very hot for at least 10 minutes following its use.",
                    "* Using a battery weaker than 6 volts will not light the bulb well. Using a battery stronger than 6 volts could be dangerous because of weak construction.",
                    "* The filament (the twisted iron wire) might move when putting the cork stopper into the glass jar. Make sure the components are in place before stopping the jar completely.",
                    "* Glass jar",
                    "* Fitted cork stopper",
                    "* 1 inch (2.54 cm) nail",
                    "* 3 feet (0.9144 m) shielded copper wire",
