            "exact_contribution": {
                "added": [
                    "",
                    "",
                    "",
                    "# Cut the copper wire. You need 2 strands about 1.5 feet (0.4572 m) long.",
                    "#* Use small wire cable cutters to cut the copper wire.",
                    "# Remove 1 inch (2.54 cm) of shielding from the ends of both strands.",
                    "#* The shielding is the plastic that covers the copper wire. Removing it can be achieved by carefully squeezing the cable cutter so that it cuts through the shielding but not the wire. The shielding can them be stripped from the ends with your hands.",
                    "# Use the nail to pierce 2 holes into the cork. The holes should be in the middle of the cork about 1 inch (2.54 cm) apart.",
                    "# Hold the 2 copper strands parallel to each other in the air.",
                    "# Place one end of each strand 2 inches (5.08 cm) inside the two holes drilled into the cork.",
                    "* If the light bulb doesn't light up after you've connected the copper ends to the battery, check your connections.",
                    "* Using more than 5 iron strands to make your filament will increase the brightness of your homemade light bulb.",
                    "* The filament (the twisted iron wire) might move when putting the cork stopper into the glass jar. Make sure the components are in place before stopping the jar completely.",
                    "* Do not touch the filament after it has been lit. It will be very hot for at least 10 minutes following its use.",
                    "* Using a battery weaker than 6 volts will not light the bulb well. Using a battery stronger than 6 volts could be dangerous because of weak construction.",
                    "* Glass jar",
                    "* Fitted cork stopper",
                    "* 1 inch (2.54 cm) nail",
                    "* 3 feet (0.9144 m) shielded copper wire",
